WEBVTT

00:15.480 --> 00:19.440
[Polly] There will be a war in this family
and one of you will die.

00:19.520 --> 00:22.040
Please be aware, Mr Shelby,
that the deaths of your people

00:22.120 --> 00:24.080
are your own responsibility.

00:24.160 --> 00:26.040
[Michael] Since my mother passed away

00:26.120 --> 00:27.440
Tommy and I haven't even spoken.

00:27.520 --> 00:29.800
I'm looking forward to
working with you again, Michael.

00:29.880 --> 00:33.120
That, my friend,
is the finest opium in the world.

00:33.200 --> 00:34.120
Why would you sell?

00:34.200 --> 00:37.119
[Tommy] The Irish are being difficult.
The Italians are not an option.

00:37.200 --> 00:39.040
-You're going to America?
-To Canada.

00:39.120 --> 00:40.760
To collect payment for the shipment.

00:40.840 --> 00:42.680
[Diana] Elizabeth,
you are a very lucky woman.

00:42.760 --> 00:44.840
To have each day
what I have only sampled once.

00:44.920 --> 00:47.360
[doctor] Mr Shelby,
your daughter has consumption.

00:47.440 --> 00:49.520
[Lizzie] She's gone, Tommy. She's gone.

00:49.600 --> 00:51.760
A daughter lost, a son found.

00:51.840 --> 00:53.800
This is my son. They call him Duke.

00:54.360 --> 00:57.560
[Holford] It is tuberculoma.
I am afraid it is inoperable.

00:57.640 --> 00:59.480
-How long?
-Perhaps 18 months.

00:59.560 --> 01:02.080
My associates are gonna
take care of Thomas Shelby

01:02.160 --> 01:04.000
and you are gonna give us his brother.

01:04.080 --> 01:06.600
What are Michael's real intentions
towards me, Gina?

01:06.680 --> 01:08.480
And if you lie, I will know.

01:08.560 --> 01:10.920
It is my intention to kill Tommy Shelby.

01:16.240 --> 01:17.640
[instrumental music playing]

01:37.160 --> 01:39.040
[Michael] It was the ambitions
and strategies

01:39.120 --> 01:40.560
of one man that caused this.

01:41.960 --> 01:43.880
I will take revenge on Tommy Shelby.

02:14.160 --> 02:17.720
You want a drink first or a whore first?

02:19.880 --> 02:21.480
I want to see my wife first.

02:22.240 --> 02:25.480
After you've fucked your wife,
you're going to kill a man, right?

02:57.480 --> 02:58.320
[Lizzie sniffs]

03:01.720 --> 03:02.600
[sniffs]

03:11.560 --> 03:15.000
The smoke from your daughter's funeral
is still in your clothes…

03:17.560 --> 03:19.000
and you slept with someone.

03:22.360 --> 03:23.520
Not just someone.

03:23.600 --> 03:24.480
[inhales sharply]

03:25.080 --> 03:26.040
The enemy.

03:28.000 --> 03:30.280
Every enemy we ever had in one woman.

03:34.400 --> 03:36.120
There are some things that I do--

03:36.200 --> 03:38.480
You're not so good
at lying any more, Tommy.

03:39.720 --> 03:41.720
These days, the truth gets in your eyes.

03:45.560 --> 03:48.560
-I have to go to Canada, Lizzie.
-[scoffs]

03:48.640 --> 03:52.600
-I need to know where you will go.
-See? You just accept it.

03:53.720 --> 03:54.760
You don't fight it.

03:58.120 --> 03:59.640
You are cursed, Tommy.

04:01.960 --> 04:06.200
Never to understand the limits
that other people will accept.

04:09.120 --> 04:11.720
Never to be allowed in
where everybody else is.

04:16.000 --> 04:17.680
A curse never to be lifted.

04:19.880 --> 04:21.440
I will be away, Lizzie.

04:23.880 --> 04:27.560
-And while I'm gone, I know a place--
-Always gone. Always away.

04:28.360 --> 04:29.200
[sniffles]

04:30.480 --> 04:33.840
Well, now your rings are gone.
Your rings are away.

04:35.200 --> 04:36.320
I'm already packed.

04:37.840 --> 04:38.720
[breath trembles]

04:41.000 --> 04:42.840
Now leave me to say goodbye to Ruby.

04:57.000 --> 04:59.240
[Tommy] I have to go away
for a bit, Charlie.

05:06.760 --> 05:07.760
Look at me.

05:09.520 --> 05:10.720
Hey, look at me.

05:15.680 --> 05:17.440
Mum already told me she's leaving.

05:18.960 --> 05:20.280
And she told me why.

05:31.360 --> 05:33.440
Mum, where are you going?

05:35.120 --> 05:35.960
[Lizzie sighs]

05:36.960 --> 05:38.200
A hotel.

05:38.800 --> 05:41.360
And then your father will get me a house.

05:46.880 --> 05:48.000
Mum,

05:48.920 --> 05:50.040
I'll come with you.

05:51.280 --> 05:52.720
I'd rather be with you.

05:53.640 --> 05:54.640
Wherever it is.

05:56.440 --> 05:57.480
You're not my mum,

05:59.200 --> 06:01.200
but you're more my mum than he's my dad.

06:03.800 --> 06:04.840
He's never here.

06:07.280 --> 06:09.120
I'd be on my own here.

06:10.040 --> 06:11.400
[Lizzie] Oh, Charles, love.

06:13.720 --> 06:15.840
I don't think your father
would allow that.

06:16.720 --> 06:18.120
[horse sighs and stomps]

06:19.880 --> 06:20.800
You can go.

06:22.480 --> 06:23.320
You can go, son.

06:25.000 --> 06:28.160
I know a good place, Lizzie.
I'll arrange that place.

06:30.120 --> 06:31.920
And, Charlie, you can take him, eh?

06:33.320 --> 06:35.200
They have stables at this new place.

06:36.200 --> 06:38.920
After a while, he'll listen to you.

06:39.000 --> 06:40.240
He'll forget about Ruby.

06:41.760 --> 06:43.040
That's how horses are.

06:45.440 --> 06:46.920
And you'll be here all alone?

06:48.800 --> 06:51.080
I'm buying land, Lizzie.
I'm buying up land.

06:52.040 --> 06:55.680
This place I've bought, I was going to
knock down, but you can go there.

06:55.760 --> 06:56.600
Dad…

06:59.600 --> 07:00.680
Where will you go?

07:09.280 --> 07:11.080
This is the Peaky Blinders' armoury.

07:12.960 --> 07:16.840
We have a very good relationship
with the BSA factory in Armoury Road.

07:18.880 --> 07:22.920
Two dozen machine guns,
half a dozen submachine guns,

07:23.560 --> 07:27.000
BSA sniper rifles,
three boxes of hand grenades.

07:27.080 --> 07:28.040
For what purpose?

07:31.040 --> 07:33.760
For eventualities like the one
that is about to occur.

07:35.480 --> 07:38.960
When men come to us with bad intentions,
family come together.

07:39.880 --> 07:42.000
Tommy says it's time
you joined the family.

07:43.840 --> 07:45.960
But you're not just going to be a soldier.

07:46.920 --> 07:49.720
You're going to be a general… someday.

07:56.600 --> 07:58.480
So, I need to ask you some questions.

08:05.840 --> 08:07.120
What have you ever fired?

08:11.320 --> 08:12.280
[Duke] Shotgun.

08:14.520 --> 08:16.840
-[gun clicks]
-Pistol. .22.

08:18.920 --> 08:20.280
What have you ever killed?

08:21.680 --> 08:22.680
A few rabbits.

08:23.520 --> 08:25.400
Pheasant, partridge, stag.

08:28.520 --> 08:29.360
Arthur tells me,

08:29.440 --> 08:32.600
when they were taking care
of some business at the betting shop,

08:32.680 --> 08:33.760
you ran away.

08:35.320 --> 08:36.560
It was unfair.

08:39.640 --> 08:41.840
Fairness is not a soldier's concern.

08:42.880 --> 08:44.159
You do what you do.

08:46.679 --> 08:47.840
I already have done.

08:48.960 --> 08:49.920
Fair and square.

08:51.520 --> 08:52.840
I have killed a man.

08:55.080 --> 08:56.280
Tommy's always right.

09:03.840 --> 09:06.760
We were outside a hospital in Bridgnorth.
In the Black Country.

09:07.920 --> 09:09.000
My mother was dying.

09:10.640 --> 09:13.280
And the orderly wouldn't give her a bed.

09:14.040 --> 09:15.120
She was a Gypsy.

09:15.680 --> 09:16.800
She had no insurance.

09:19.680 --> 09:21.000
She never saw the sunrise.

09:23.840 --> 09:25.440
Nor did that man who denied her.

09:30.320 --> 09:32.640
Just one more thing
we need to know about you.

09:37.280 --> 09:38.480
Can you keep a secret?

09:40.800 --> 09:41.640
[door slams]

09:44.800 --> 09:46.080
[Arthur] I know, brother.

09:56.800 --> 09:57.800
I know.

10:02.920 --> 10:03.920
I know.

10:05.480 --> 10:06.760
I stole your keys.

10:12.080 --> 10:13.120
Tuberculoma.

10:16.880 --> 10:17.880
In your brain.

10:18.720 --> 10:22.360
[smacks lips] Yeah. But I still have time
to do what I need to do.

10:26.600 --> 10:27.640
Fuck you, Tommy.

10:28.840 --> 10:30.680
I don't need anyone to know, Arthur.

10:32.760 --> 10:34.040
No, you don't, do ya?

10:34.760 --> 10:37.800
-You don't need anything, do ya?
-No, I don't need anything.

10:37.880 --> 10:39.000
I don't need anything.

10:39.840 --> 10:41.720
How long have we been dead for, eh?

10:42.400 --> 10:43.600
You and me. How long?

10:44.520 --> 10:46.880
-At least now I'll have a certificate.
-[scoffs]

10:47.720 --> 10:50.800
Wherever it is, I'll get the drinks in
and I'll wait for you.

10:55.160 --> 10:56.960
-Fuck's sake.
-Yeah.

10:58.160 --> 10:59.920
All them bullets that missed.

11:01.120 --> 11:02.320
It's funny, Arthur.

11:03.480 --> 11:04.760
It's funny is what it is.

11:07.360 --> 11:08.680
So don't you fucking weep.

11:12.680 --> 11:13.560
Weep.

11:15.360 --> 11:19.200
When everyone is taken care of financially
I'll take myself away. On my own.

11:24.080 --> 11:25.600
I don't want anyone… [inhales]

11:28.080 --> 11:31.360
Anyone who may or may not love me…

11:33.040 --> 11:34.360
to have to see me crawl…

11:36.560 --> 11:38.320
and grow insane and helpless.

11:39.200 --> 11:42.000
That would be a cruelty to me and to them.

11:43.960 --> 11:46.880
By the time people know the truth,

11:47.720 --> 11:48.720
I will be gone.

11:51.160 --> 11:52.240
What about Lizzie?

11:53.640 --> 11:56.760
I have some papers I need you to sign
on behalf of the company.

11:57.960 --> 11:58.960
Told Lizzie?

11:59.880 --> 12:02.040
I'm working with the housing minister.

12:02.120 --> 12:03.920
I will be allocating contracts,

12:04.000 --> 12:06.360
construction contracts,
worth ten million pounds.

12:06.440 --> 12:08.120
You haven't told Lizzie?

12:08.200 --> 12:11.800
Some contracts I'll be allocating are with
companies in which we have an interest--

12:11.880 --> 12:14.520
Fuck you and your contracts!

12:14.600 --> 12:17.480
So the Shelby Company Limited
will continue to earn money.

12:19.280 --> 12:22.200
But mostly, Arthur, I'm doing it
because it's a good thing.

12:23.560 --> 12:25.320
-Building houses.
-Oh.

12:25.400 --> 12:28.680
-Yeah, for ordinary working people.
-Yeah. Good for you. Fucking--

12:28.760 --> 12:30.880
[Tommy] In the interests
of a fairer future.

12:31.760 --> 12:32.800
Before that,

12:33.640 --> 12:35.360
I will be going to Canada

12:36.400 --> 12:38.720
to collect payment for the shipment.
Five million pounds!

12:38.800 --> 12:40.440
Five fucking million!

12:40.520 --> 12:43.960
Which I will share
among the Shelby family.

12:46.200 --> 12:47.800
And that will be my legacy.

12:47.880 --> 12:50.160
Instead of me, there will be money.

12:51.040 --> 12:54.280
Because for most of the people
who are close to me, that is what I am!

12:54.920 --> 12:57.480
Fucking money. That is my agency.

12:57.560 --> 13:00.160
Is that all you think you are, eh? Hmm?

13:02.480 --> 13:03.360
Stand up.

13:07.680 --> 13:08.680
You heard me.

13:10.120 --> 13:12.600
Stand up. On your feet.

13:14.360 --> 13:15.560
-On your fucking feet.
-Arthur.

13:15.640 --> 13:17.920
On your feet, soldier. On your feet.

13:18.400 --> 13:20.200
Stand the fuck up! Come here! [grunts]

13:20.280 --> 13:21.200
Arthur!

13:23.560 --> 13:25.800
No! Enough!

13:27.720 --> 13:29.920
You hear me? Enough!

13:32.520 --> 13:33.400
Enough!

13:41.520 --> 13:42.560
Now you know.

13:44.920 --> 13:46.240
You tell no one else

13:48.040 --> 13:49.360
until I'm gone.

13:49.440 --> 13:50.680
Until you're gone, yeah.

13:51.280 --> 13:53.160
[Arthur breathing heavily]

13:54.120 --> 13:56.560
When the time comes, I'll call you.

14:00.480 --> 14:02.560
I'll tell you where. It'll be a wagon.

14:03.320 --> 14:04.760
Fuck your wagon!

14:05.960 --> 14:07.280
You light the flame.

14:07.360 --> 14:10.840
You bring Charlie
and Curly and no one else.

14:12.160 --> 14:13.120
Get drunk.

14:13.840 --> 14:15.960
Rake the ashes for silver and gold.

14:16.040 --> 14:17.400
Fuck you!

14:18.600 --> 14:20.200
And your fucking plans!

14:35.640 --> 14:37.600
That time I did let you fucking win.

14:39.720 --> 14:40.560
[groans]

14:46.560 --> 14:47.440
John.

14:48.200 --> 14:49.120
[glass thuds]

14:50.960 --> 14:52.280
[Arthur] Fuck you, John.

14:55.480 --> 14:58.000
[sobbing] Fucking both of you.

14:59.720 --> 15:02.640
Arthur. Arthur.

15:04.840 --> 15:11.760
Come here. Come here.
Come here. Come here.

15:13.840 --> 15:16.680
-Let me see your eyes.
-I'm clean, man.

15:17.560 --> 15:19.640
The dragon's fucking gone.

15:20.400 --> 15:23.240
Thanks to you.
Fucking thanks to you. [sobs]

15:23.320 --> 15:25.520
[emotional music playing]

15:51.040 --> 15:53.400
You all right? Come on.

15:55.440 --> 15:56.520
You're fucking--

15:56.600 --> 15:59.680
Hey, I am still fucking here.
Pull yourself together, come on.

16:00.200 --> 16:01.320
We have work to do.

16:03.360 --> 16:04.320
Come on!

16:09.400 --> 16:10.560
[indistinct shouting]

16:19.360 --> 16:20.200
[door opens]

16:23.360 --> 16:24.320
[door closes]

16:25.360 --> 16:26.520
[footsteps approaching]

16:28.280 --> 16:31.120
Are you sure you want Billy?
I had to shut up the shop.

16:31.600 --> 16:33.240
[Tommy] Yes. We want Billy.

16:33.840 --> 16:35.120
[Arthur] Sit down, Billy.

16:40.960 --> 16:43.000
Thank you for inviting me, Mr Shelby.

16:45.280 --> 16:46.600
[Arthur] Good to see you again.

16:54.040 --> 16:54.880
[Finn] No.

16:54.960 --> 16:56.920
Mary says not until after six o'clock.

17:03.000 --> 17:06.040
He said to tell his father
he feels okay about it.

17:06.120 --> 17:07.080
[Tommy] Good.

17:07.920 --> 17:09.079
Shut the door, Duke.

17:18.880 --> 17:22.880
Now, we are all gathered, and those…

17:22.960 --> 17:24.400
[in Romani] who know the truth…

17:26.560 --> 17:27.960
will know to be cautious.

17:28.640 --> 17:31.760
[in English] Apologies, Mr Shelby,
I still don't speak the lingo.

17:33.000 --> 17:35.800
[Tommy] Well, Finn here
never even bothered to learn it.

17:36.280 --> 17:38.680
I heard "tachipen". Truth.

17:39.320 --> 17:41.000
You said something about the truth.

17:41.080 --> 17:42.960
[Tommy] Truth. The truth is

17:44.000 --> 17:45.880
I called men here that I could trust

17:47.200 --> 17:48.840
because I will be going away.

17:50.760 --> 17:53.160
I have to collect payment
for a shipment of goods

17:53.240 --> 17:55.000
which left Liverpool ten days ago.

17:55.480 --> 17:56.480
[Finn] Payment from who?

17:57.640 --> 17:59.520
[Tommy] South Boston Irish, Finn.

18:00.840 --> 18:01.880
Bootleggers.

18:04.600 --> 18:05.640
Are you going alone?

18:07.240 --> 18:09.680
Johnny Dogs already sailed for Canada.

18:09.760 --> 18:10.880
Michael will be there.

18:12.280 --> 18:13.440
Michael is family.

18:14.400 --> 18:16.480
And Michael will be
my guarantee of safety.

18:17.880 --> 18:19.800
While I'm away, I have a job for you all.

18:20.320 --> 18:22.160
I need you to go to Arrow House.

18:22.840 --> 18:27.320
I will be leaving Arrow House for good.
And there are things that need removing.

18:27.400 --> 18:28.840
I need men that I can trust.

18:29.800 --> 18:31.600
There is cash. There is valuables.

18:32.240 --> 18:35.960
There's information about important people
that has more value than gold.

18:38.120 --> 18:41.280
There are also
bodies buried on the grounds

18:41.360 --> 18:44.520
which need digging up
before the contractors start moving earth.

18:44.600 --> 18:46.800
Isiah, you'll be in charge.

18:48.280 --> 18:49.960
In Arrow House, there is a wine cellar.

18:50.040 --> 18:52.880
In that wine cellar,
there are fine French wines

18:52.960 --> 18:54.880
that are worth more than a man's life.

18:55.800 --> 18:58.240
You're welcome to them, boys.
It'll be like a…

18:58.320 --> 18:59.920
Like a farewell party.

19:01.920 --> 19:03.160
You ready for the party, son?

19:05.000 --> 19:06.320
[in Romani] I know the truth.

19:08.160 --> 19:09.440
[Finn in English] "Tachipen".

19:10.080 --> 19:11.760
The fucking truth again.

19:13.560 --> 19:14.440
What truth?

19:14.520 --> 19:16.120
You'll need shovels, you'll need boxes

19:16.200 --> 19:20.080
and you'll take the bones to Mr Patches
to put in the furnace at Greenhams.

19:21.280 --> 19:22.200
Got it?

19:23.400 --> 19:25.000
All right. Any questions?

19:25.080 --> 19:27.440
Yeah. If it's a party, can we bring girls?
[chuckles]

19:28.840 --> 19:30.080
[Tommy] No, Billy.

19:30.160 --> 19:31.720
All the fun will be laid on for you.

19:34.360 --> 19:35.800
So when is the party, Tom?

19:41.320 --> 19:42.320
Mr Shelby.

19:44.760 --> 19:46.200
Party's next Sunday, Billy.

19:47.840 --> 19:49.520
You mean this Sunday?

19:50.200 --> 19:51.080
Yeah.

19:51.560 --> 19:53.720
[Arthur] While you're digging
fucking holes,

19:54.560 --> 19:57.440
I'll be here
drinking champagne with my wife.

19:57.520 --> 19:59.240
It's our wedding anniversary.

19:59.960 --> 20:00.880
Right.

20:00.960 --> 20:02.080
[Tommy] Oh, and, Finn…

20:03.000 --> 20:05.720
By the way, please explain to, um…

20:06.680 --> 20:07.640
What's her name?

20:07.720 --> 20:08.800
-[Finn] Mary.
-Mary?

20:08.880 --> 20:10.120
-[Finn] Yes.
-Is it Mary?

20:10.640 --> 20:13.680
Please explain to Mary
that you are a Shelby.

20:14.240 --> 20:17.800
It says it here on the back
of your watch. Have a look. Shelby.

20:17.880 --> 20:18.840
Look.

20:19.520 --> 20:23.360
This means you own the watch,
the watch doesn't own you.

20:24.280 --> 20:26.760
The clock strikes six
when you fucking tell it to.

20:27.560 --> 20:28.640
Have a whiskey.

20:30.520 --> 20:31.960
Enjoy the party, boys.

20:35.680 --> 20:36.760
[jazz music playing]

20:47.000 --> 20:47.840
[Gina sighs]

20:48.440 --> 20:49.800
You want a drink, baby?

20:49.880 --> 20:50.720
No.

20:51.760 --> 20:54.480
-Drinking water like Tommy, huh?
-[sighs]

20:56.000 --> 20:58.280
Until this thing is done,
I need a clear head.

20:58.360 --> 20:59.200
[liquid pours]

21:04.240 --> 21:05.360
[telephone ringing]

21:07.400 --> 21:08.240
Leave it.

21:23.360 --> 21:24.360
Yeah.

21:26.400 --> 21:27.360
Good.

21:28.080 --> 21:29.080
That's good.

21:31.000 --> 21:32.120
Look, I've got to go.

21:34.680 --> 21:35.680
Good news, Michael.

21:36.360 --> 21:37.280
Listen.

21:39.760 --> 21:41.640
That was our informant in Birmingham.

21:43.240 --> 21:45.880
The Shelby men
will all be together on Sunday.

21:47.080 --> 21:48.960
But Arthur will be
having dinner with his wife

21:49.040 --> 21:50.760
at the bar at The Garrison Tavern.

21:57.320 --> 22:00.400
As I recall, the Shelby table
is right next to the windows, correct?

22:00.480 --> 22:02.360
Every table's a Shelby table.

22:02.440 --> 22:03.400
Yes, but…

22:04.880 --> 22:07.680
Maybe our people could just drive by

22:08.320 --> 22:11.280
and shoot Arthur through the glass
without even getting out of the car.

22:13.880 --> 22:14.800
Michael.

22:16.600 --> 22:19.000
We've talked about this.
There's no other choice.

22:19.080 --> 22:21.640
This business is between me and Tommy.

22:21.720 --> 22:22.560
Yes.

22:23.120 --> 22:27.040
And when you kill Tommy,
Arthur will come after you.

22:28.560 --> 22:29.680
He has to die too.

22:33.040 --> 22:34.960
If Arthur's in a bar, he'll be drunk.

22:36.720 --> 22:37.720
Or worse.

22:39.360 --> 22:41.360
At least he'll die without pain. [sighs]

22:42.120 --> 22:43.240
[lighter clicking]

22:47.800 --> 22:49.080
Who'll do the killing?

22:51.480 --> 22:53.960
Tommy's working with a faction of the IRA.

22:54.560 --> 22:55.880
Connor has connections.

22:56.600 --> 22:57.600
They made a deal.

22:59.160 --> 23:01.360
A favour in return for guns.

23:03.920 --> 23:05.200
But, Michael…

23:07.120 --> 23:09.000
whilst the assassin's in the city…

23:11.160 --> 23:12.000
Tommy has a son.

23:13.080 --> 23:14.160
He's a kid.

23:14.880 --> 23:15.800
Kids grow up.

23:16.760 --> 23:18.960
We don't kill women
and we don't kill kids.

23:21.360 --> 23:23.960
The informant also mentioned
a new boy named Duke.

23:24.040 --> 23:25.960
Do you want a fucking bloodbath, Gina?

23:28.280 --> 23:29.640
I know about the new boy.

23:30.840 --> 23:34.360
I've decided that the illegitimate son
is not a threat. My decision.

23:37.160 --> 23:38.160
Only Arthur.

23:40.800 --> 23:41.800
Michael, baby.

23:43.320 --> 23:44.720
Everything's been agreed.

23:44.800 --> 23:45.760
[cigarette fizzles]

23:48.040 --> 23:50.120
Everybody wants the same things.

23:54.880 --> 23:57.960
How many men do you think
they killed with bullets and blades?

23:58.520 --> 23:59.520
[Michael sighs]

23:59.600 --> 24:01.560
That's how Tommy became king.

24:03.320 --> 24:04.640
And in three days' time,

24:05.760 --> 24:07.880
that's how you will become king.

24:10.760 --> 24:13.200
Deep down, Arthur and Tommy
wanna be dead anyway.

24:15.760 --> 24:17.400
On Sunday, we'll just…

24:20.840 --> 24:22.120
give them what they want.

24:26.320 --> 24:27.640
[tense music playing]

24:29.680 --> 24:30.880
[footsteps approaching]

24:45.960 --> 24:46.800
[door opens]

24:47.920 --> 24:48.760
[door closes]

24:48.840 --> 24:50.520
[Diana] Oswald was called away.

24:50.600 --> 24:51.920
He sent me instead.

24:54.640 --> 24:56.320
Actually, that's not true.

24:56.400 --> 24:59.920
I sent Oswald away and elected myself
to be his representative.

25:01.520 --> 25:02.800
What was it you wanted?

25:04.600 --> 25:07.760
[Tommy] I'm planning on bringing
my housing bill before Parliament.

25:07.840 --> 25:10.160
You'll need to start drawing up a list

25:10.240 --> 25:14.080
of all your land-owning families
with gambling debts, drug addictions,

25:14.160 --> 25:16.240
any other drain on their resources.

25:16.320 --> 25:18.680
I will deliver offers
to buy the surplus land

25:19.680 --> 25:20.640
using treasury bonds.

25:20.720 --> 25:22.360
Thomas, why don't we fuck here.

25:23.080 --> 25:24.120
On these benches.

25:25.600 --> 25:26.520
Right now.

25:28.600 --> 25:29.880
We wouldn't be the first.

25:32.640 --> 25:34.040
I hear your wife left you.

25:42.600 --> 25:46.720
Over the last few months,
I've had some associates of mine

25:48.520 --> 25:50.520
break into some of your pals' houses.

25:50.600 --> 25:52.240
They stole paperwork.

25:52.320 --> 25:55.320
Letters, bills, bank statements--

25:55.400 --> 25:56.520
Are you not upset?

25:57.240 --> 25:58.080
[clicks tongue]

26:00.320 --> 26:01.360
This is a list

26:02.280 --> 26:06.040
of all land-owning families
facing foreclosure.

26:10.600 --> 26:11.680
[Tommy sighs]

26:11.760 --> 26:13.440
And to answer your question…

26:17.160 --> 26:18.000
No.

26:20.800 --> 26:23.040
No, I am not upset that my wife left me.

26:25.360 --> 26:27.480
And, yeah, if you want to fuck, I'll fuck.

26:28.160 --> 26:32.000
But you'll have to cross the floor
'cause I refuse to fuck on Tory benches.

26:47.320 --> 26:48.400
Mr Shelby.

26:51.440 --> 26:55.640
I was going to have this delivered to you,
but I decided to bring it in person.

26:59.640 --> 27:02.280
It's an invitation
to mine and Diana's wedding.

27:03.480 --> 27:04.520
It's in Berlin.

27:05.960 --> 27:09.200
We're going to get married
in the presence of the Führer himself.

27:15.000 --> 27:16.320
Were you having fun?

27:17.200 --> 27:18.760
Making paper aeroplanes.

27:20.560 --> 27:24.840
I'm afraid… [sighs] I have business.
I will be in Canada.

27:28.080 --> 27:28.920
Pity.

27:33.920 --> 27:35.360
Oh, and, uh…

27:36.320 --> 27:39.720
the other reason I wanted to…
bring this in person

27:39.800 --> 27:43.480
was to tell you that after our wedding,
you must understand, Mr Shelby,

27:44.880 --> 27:47.520
that if you so much
as look in my wife's direction,

27:48.200 --> 27:49.560
I will have you killed.

27:54.120 --> 27:55.160
Come, Diana.

27:58.400 --> 27:59.400
Just think,

28:00.240 --> 28:04.680
very soon, crumbling old institutions
like this one will be swept away

28:04.760 --> 28:06.840
and become a thing of ancient memory.

28:09.400 --> 28:10.400
Fly safe.

28:32.280 --> 28:33.120
[sighs]

29:02.040 --> 29:03.280
[inaudible conversation]

29:18.720 --> 29:20.160
Be careful with this baby.

29:21.760 --> 29:22.920
You see any potholes,

29:24.800 --> 29:26.040
you drive round them.

29:38.360 --> 29:39.200
[engine starts]

29:45.000 --> 29:47.400
[Frances] Mr Shelby called to say
to expect you.

29:48.280 --> 29:50.440
Yeah, we've come to do a bit of gardening.

29:50.520 --> 29:53.160
We're hearing so many rumours
about what's happening to the house.

29:53.240 --> 29:57.160
Tommy says your second-best quality,
after your baking,

29:57.240 --> 29:58.720
is you don't ask questions.

30:02.360 --> 30:04.680
Get everybody away
from the house until Monday.

30:06.840 --> 30:10.680
Okay. Let's find these bottles of wine
worth more than a man's life.

30:52.880 --> 30:53.800
[glasses clinking]

31:05.400 --> 31:06.920
There's only one guest here.

31:07.000 --> 31:10.320
The rest of the rooms are free
if you want to use them while you wait.

31:10.800 --> 31:13.240
Our friend will be here
by the time it gets dark.

31:14.280 --> 31:15.920
There was a storm last night.

31:16.000 --> 31:17.200
Last of a hurricane.

31:18.040 --> 31:19.120
Boats all came in.

31:20.680 --> 31:22.960
He's not coming by boat,
he's coming by plane.

31:25.280 --> 31:28.160
Then your friend is dead. Wind was like…

31:28.240 --> 31:29.400
[imitates wind howling]

31:30.480 --> 31:32.640
Maybe God's done your job for you, Mickey.

31:32.720 --> 31:35.640
My name is not fucking Mickey,
there is no fucking God

31:35.720 --> 31:37.120
and Tommy will be here.

31:41.800 --> 31:42.760
Another one.

31:43.760 --> 31:44.760
[thunder claps]

31:54.480 --> 31:55.960
[Polly] There will be a war

31:57.560 --> 31:59.160
and one of you will die.

32:00.760 --> 32:02.520
Which one, I cannot tell.

32:02.600 --> 32:04.400
[Nelson] You're a brave man, Mr Shelby.

32:04.480 --> 32:05.320
[breathing heavily]

32:05.400 --> 32:06.760
[Lizzie] Where the fuck were you?

32:07.960 --> 32:10.360
She's gone, Tommy. She's gone.

32:11.160 --> 32:13.480
[Tommy] The devils
who did this will pay, Ruby.

32:13.560 --> 32:16.520
[Holford] Tuberculoma.
I am afraid it is inoperable.

32:18.840 --> 32:21.240
-[Tommy] How long?
-[Holford] Perhaps 18 months.

32:21.320 --> 32:23.560
[Tommy] I will change. Change for good.

32:23.640 --> 32:25.960
[Lizzie] What is this "good"
that you will become?!

32:26.040 --> 32:29.240
Kill and kill…

32:30.440 --> 32:31.880
[aircraft rattles]

32:56.800 --> 32:58.280
[indistinct chattering]

33:02.800 --> 33:03.880
[Finn] What's going on?

33:03.960 --> 33:05.400
[Billy and Finn laughing]

33:05.480 --> 33:06.600
Hey.

33:06.680 --> 33:08.240
-Hey. Hey.
-[Finn coughs and sniffs]

33:08.320 --> 33:11.720
What the fuck is this? I thought
it was meant to be a fucking party, lads.

33:11.800 --> 33:13.160
It is, now you're here.

33:13.240 --> 33:15.440
[hesitates] Where's the fucking booze?

33:15.520 --> 33:16.800
[Duke] In the kitchen.

33:16.880 --> 33:18.560
All the booze is in the kitchen.

33:19.320 --> 33:20.280
[Billy] All right.

33:31.840 --> 33:37.160
[Lazarus] God gives a man wealth,
possessions and honour.

33:37.240 --> 33:43.120
But God steps in and says,
"No! This is grievous, mindless evil!"

33:43.200 --> 33:45.480
Where is he? Jeremiah?

33:45.560 --> 33:47.640
In heaven, looking down.

33:47.720 --> 33:48.640
[coins clink]

33:51.600 --> 33:55.800
God tells us the blood
is given to Him from us…

33:56.520 --> 33:58.880
[Finn] Why don't you turn
the fucking lights on?

33:58.960 --> 34:02.440
[Isiah] There's no longer any power
in the house of Thomas Shelby.

34:03.120 --> 34:05.720
[Finn] Why not?
What do you mean? What happened?

34:06.720 --> 34:08.600
[Billy] I thought
there would be girls here.

34:08.680 --> 34:11.280
[Duke] Who need girls
when you're in a house bound for hell?

34:11.360 --> 34:12.520
[Finn] Fuck do you mean?

34:14.760 --> 34:16.880
Hey! What the fuck do you mean?

34:21.719 --> 34:22.679
[gun cocks]

34:27.000 --> 34:28.440
[Billy] Fuck!

34:29.199 --> 34:30.040
Fuck!

34:30.120 --> 34:32.199
We can do whatever we want in this house.

34:32.840 --> 34:34.400
It's got a death sentence.

34:35.440 --> 34:36.440
[scoffs]

34:39.719 --> 34:43.719
I don't want a drink. I want to go
dig up those fucking bodies, yeah?

34:44.480 --> 34:45.600
-Billy?
-Yeah.

34:45.679 --> 34:47.400
Got to wait until
all the bodies are buried

34:47.480 --> 34:49.320
before you start digging them back up.

34:50.239 --> 34:52.320
What the fuck does that mean?

34:53.960 --> 34:55.719
I'm a fucking Shelby.

34:57.760 --> 34:58.760
So am I.

35:21.320 --> 35:22.320
He's here.

35:25.600 --> 35:26.760
[aircraft rattling]

36:03.080 --> 36:03.920
[exhales deeply]

36:04.800 --> 36:07.240
Step back and give me
a bit of light there, boys.

36:48.920 --> 36:49.920
[exhales]

37:07.040 --> 37:10.800
The charge is set to blow in 30 minutes.
That's at exactly 16:20.

37:10.880 --> 37:11.920
Everyone got that?

37:16.720 --> 37:17.720
I'll do it.

37:19.720 --> 37:21.320
This is between me and Tommy.

37:21.960 --> 37:23.360
I'll do it with my own hand.

37:25.200 --> 37:26.360
I'll come with you.

37:32.040 --> 37:33.680
Yeah, don't slam any doors.

37:37.000 --> 37:37.960
[door closes]

37:49.200 --> 37:50.160
Easy.

37:52.760 --> 37:53.800
[car boot clicks]

37:56.000 --> 37:59.760
It's just a pity you didn't have the guts
to shoot him face-to-face.

38:00.960 --> 38:03.920
My mother was a Gypsy. She saw the future.

38:05.440 --> 38:08.680
She always said it won't be
a bullet that will kill Tommy Shelby.

38:13.160 --> 38:14.920
[Connor] Hey, lads.

38:16.040 --> 38:17.360
Over by the bridge.

38:17.440 --> 38:19.280
Big, big fish.

38:19.800 --> 38:21.680
[in French] Fish. Big.

38:22.520 --> 38:23.480
[in English] Go on.

38:26.080 --> 38:27.160
[breathing heavily]

38:28.120 --> 38:29.440
[Duke] Take the gun, Finn.

38:31.960 --> 38:33.720
Arthur says if you don't do it

38:34.320 --> 38:36.320
then you can
walk away from this family for good.

38:36.400 --> 38:38.720
What the fuck do you know about family?

38:38.800 --> 38:40.440
You're not family.

38:40.960 --> 38:43.440
You're the son of a fucking whore.

38:47.080 --> 38:49.360
[Duke] Just take the gun and do it, Finn.

38:49.440 --> 38:51.520
[Billy whimpering] Take the fucking gun.

39:00.480 --> 39:02.680
Now you have the gun, Finn.

39:02.760 --> 39:04.120
You have the gun.

39:04.200 --> 39:05.640
Use it on these fucks.

39:06.320 --> 39:07.200
[grunts]

39:13.520 --> 39:14.520
[gun clicks]

39:18.040 --> 39:20.160
[grunting]

39:21.920 --> 39:23.360
[Duke] Charlie Strong told me,

39:24.080 --> 39:25.680
"When you give Finn the gun,

39:25.760 --> 39:28.480
make sure the first
two chambers are empty." [chuckles]

39:29.440 --> 39:30.880
Good old Uncle Charlie.

39:40.440 --> 39:41.360
[breath trembling]

39:52.560 --> 39:55.520
You are no longer a member
of this Shelby family.

39:57.440 --> 40:00.680
By order of the Peaky fucking Blinders.

40:01.760 --> 40:03.480
[Finn] I will come for you.

40:05.080 --> 40:07.080
I will fucking come for you!

40:08.120 --> 40:09.360
[breathing heavily]

40:53.880 --> 40:55.640
[Lazarus] …that find me faulting,

40:55.720 --> 41:00.440
them, who govern like dogs
in Garrison Lane and Artillery.

41:00.520 --> 41:05.240
Hear this. Then came Jesus forth,
wearing the crown of thorns

41:05.320 --> 41:08.400
and a purple robe, and Pilate said,

41:08.480 --> 41:12.000
"Behold the man. He is the man."

41:12.080 --> 41:14.160
Not the Peaky Blinders.

41:14.240 --> 41:18.160
We see them in their automobiles,
with their whores…

41:19.240 --> 41:22.560
…and their pity for us.
Cast down…

41:24.240 --> 41:25.520
[watch ticking]

41:25.600 --> 41:27.840
[Arthur grunts]

41:27.920 --> 41:30.360
[Lazarus continues preaching
indistinctly]

41:33.320 --> 41:34.880
[telephone ringing]

41:42.160 --> 41:43.040
[door opens]

41:56.200 --> 41:57.680
[telephone continues ringing]

42:13.840 --> 42:14.760
[ringing stops]

42:34.440 --> 42:35.280
[gun cocks]

42:37.560 --> 42:38.720
Order your man to drop it.

42:39.480 --> 42:40.480
Order him.

42:41.960 --> 42:43.640
Empty the fucking gun. Tell him.

42:47.160 --> 42:48.320
[bullets clatter]

42:50.760 --> 42:53.120
-[Arthur] You all right, Charlie?
-All good here, Arthur.

42:53.800 --> 42:54.920
Let's move.

42:55.520 --> 42:58.360
Take you out to the street.
I don't wanna spoil my pub.

43:10.160 --> 43:12.160
You'd shoot us like dogs?

43:12.240 --> 43:13.720
No, I don't shoot dogs.

43:13.800 --> 43:16.080
I shoot fucking fascists. Move.

43:17.760 --> 43:18.760
[gunshot fires]

43:40.440 --> 43:41.960
[crackling]

43:56.160 --> 43:57.040
[footsteps echo]

44:28.480 --> 44:29.320
[footsteps]

44:49.920 --> 44:51.000
[exhales]

45:03.840 --> 45:04.760
[gun cocks]

45:19.760 --> 45:20.640
Fuck.

45:25.800 --> 45:26.640
[body thuds]

45:33.280 --> 45:34.120
[gasps]

45:43.160 --> 45:44.040
[Laura whistles]

46:34.440 --> 46:35.400
Oh, Lord!

46:36.000 --> 46:39.800
Time for the chosen one to reveal himself!

46:57.040 --> 46:58.080
[breathing heavily]

47:00.320 --> 47:01.480
[baby crying]

47:04.000 --> 47:05.400
[kid shouting indistinctly]

47:17.480 --> 47:19.480
[woman] No, kids, no. Come here.

47:19.560 --> 47:21.000
I said come here!

47:21.080 --> 47:24.160
Come here now.
What have I told you about running off?

47:24.240 --> 47:26.240
Don't. Put it down.

47:26.320 --> 47:27.400
Come here, come on!

47:34.560 --> 47:36.600
-Emily? Emily, come on!
-[metal clinks]

47:37.200 --> 47:40.320
If you get lost in the fog,
the Peaky Blinders will get you.

47:40.400 --> 47:41.240
[baby crying]

47:43.320 --> 47:44.400
[Arthur] Jeremiah.

47:45.760 --> 47:49.720
Let's show 'em the old keepsake
from Passchendaele.

47:58.320 --> 47:59.400
[rattling]

48:07.040 --> 48:08.080
Fuck.

48:12.160 --> 48:13.560
[gasping]

48:17.200 --> 48:18.040
[coughing]

48:21.320 --> 48:22.320
[coughing]

48:50.080 --> 48:51.960
[coughing and gasping]

48:57.720 --> 48:58.760
[cannister rattles]

49:00.360 --> 49:01.760
[Laura coughing]

49:20.440 --> 49:21.320
[gasping]

49:22.840 --> 49:25.080
Come here. [shushes]

49:27.160 --> 49:28.360
[Laura gasping]

49:28.440 --> 49:30.640
Breathe. Breathe.

49:38.120 --> 49:39.920
Her name was Elizabeth Gray.

49:43.120 --> 49:44.760
She was my Aunt Polly.

49:46.400 --> 49:47.400
My Aunt Polly.

49:50.960 --> 49:52.560
Vengeance is for the Lord--

49:58.240 --> 49:59.840
Not in Small Heath, it ain't.

50:04.520 --> 50:05.840
Rest in peace, Pol.

50:39.040 --> 50:40.440
Leave us, Uncle Charlie.

50:41.360 --> 50:42.600
We're still in France.

51:25.640 --> 51:26.840
[Pat] Okay.

51:27.960 --> 51:29.600
I see him coming out of the fog.

51:37.960 --> 51:38.840
[glass thuds]

51:44.040 --> 51:45.160
[door opens]

51:48.840 --> 51:49.680
[door closes]

51:50.920 --> 51:51.960
How was the flight?

51:53.040 --> 51:55.520
[Tommy] They say it's the future.
I'm not so sure.

51:56.240 --> 51:57.120
Whiskey.

51:59.560 --> 52:00.400
[Michael coughs]

52:00.480 --> 52:01.440
Hello, Michael.

52:03.760 --> 52:04.600
Tommy.

52:06.520 --> 52:07.360
[sighs]

52:14.880 --> 52:15.840
Give me another.

52:18.800 --> 52:21.680
We want you to take us
to where the opium is being stored.

52:22.800 --> 52:26.960
[Connor] And then we will provide you
with a banker's draft for the full amount.

52:28.400 --> 52:29.480
Five million dollars.

52:31.760 --> 52:32.840
Five million dollars.

52:34.480 --> 52:35.480
[Sam] Let's go.

52:42.720 --> 52:43.920
[Michael] I'll go with Tommy.

52:44.600 --> 52:45.880
You boys follow behind.

52:52.600 --> 52:53.520
Shit.

52:54.080 --> 52:55.320
Forgot my cigarettes.

53:01.360 --> 53:02.720
[suspenseful music playing]

54:21.600 --> 54:22.600
[glass shatters]

54:46.960 --> 54:47.800
[exhales]

54:49.800 --> 54:50.760
Mum.

54:53.840 --> 54:54.840
It's done.

54:58.040 --> 54:59.040
It's over.

55:02.240 --> 55:03.640
May God forgive me.

55:18.360 --> 55:19.560
[breathing heavily]

55:38.240 --> 55:39.320
Johnny!

55:40.160 --> 55:41.480
Johnny, where are you?

55:43.800 --> 55:45.880
I switched the ticker like you said, Tom.

55:50.080 --> 55:52.160
Tell me I've done a good thing here, Tom.

56:04.080 --> 56:05.240
Goodbye, Michael.

56:05.800 --> 56:06.880
Goodbye, Johnny.

56:08.880 --> 56:09.920
You're a good man.

56:14.200 --> 56:17.680
I'm gonna go look at the fog, Tom.

56:23.920 --> 56:25.120
Speak to me.

56:27.120 --> 56:28.480
Speak to me, Michael.

56:31.920 --> 56:32.960
You killed her.

56:33.600 --> 56:35.800
-Polly made her own choices, Michael.
-No.

56:37.120 --> 56:40.600
No one close to you
makes a choice without your opinion, Tom.

56:42.960 --> 56:47.080
Not Arthur, not me, not Ada.

56:49.400 --> 56:50.840
We can't escape you.

56:54.200 --> 56:56.560
Your lethal hand
is always on our shoulders.

57:01.360 --> 57:02.600
Polly was half of me.

57:04.440 --> 57:06.000
Still visits me in my dreams.

57:08.680 --> 57:10.040
She'll visit me no more.

57:12.960 --> 57:13.800
[Michael thuds]

57:23.960 --> 57:25.480
I have no limitations.

57:42.920 --> 57:43.920
[door closes]

58:31.040 --> 58:33.880
[Alfie] I smell the smell
of roasting Irishmen.

58:34.800 --> 58:35.920
Oh, yes. Hello.

58:36.960 --> 58:39.200
-[playing piano]
-I also smell the smell of tobacco.

58:39.280 --> 58:42.400
Which is forbidden
in my presence for all except for one,

58:42.480 --> 58:44.360
my new wife, Edna.

58:45.840 --> 58:48.680
The Irish being rendered smoke and fat,

58:49.240 --> 58:51.440
I now own half of Boston.

58:51.520 --> 58:56.440
So, out of respect
for my restored authority,

58:58.280 --> 59:00.640
put the fucking cigarette out now, Tommy.

59:02.680 --> 59:03.680
Hello, Alfie.

59:04.520 --> 59:05.960
I heard it was a good wedding.

59:06.040 --> 59:07.760
Yeah it was, actually. Thank you.

59:08.360 --> 59:10.520
Edna's from a family circus.

59:10.600 --> 59:13.280
So, after the ketubah
and the old swapping of rings

59:13.360 --> 59:17.360
and the smashing of glass,
we left aboard elephants.

59:17.440 --> 59:18.760
Yeah. It was quite a thing.

59:18.840 --> 59:20.720
They had to shut down Camden High Street,

59:20.800 --> 59:23.320
and even the gentile,
what normally fucking hate me,

59:23.400 --> 59:25.080
they waved with their hankies.

59:27.560 --> 59:28.520
Justice.

59:30.680 --> 59:32.360
And housekeeping.

59:32.440 --> 59:34.480
Long overdue.

59:35.560 --> 59:39.240
Yeah, look at that little cunt ascending,
he is ascending to the heavens.

59:39.320 --> 59:41.680
Right in front of us.
Before our very eyes.

59:41.760 --> 59:43.840
And I can see with this eye.
I'm not blind.

59:43.920 --> 59:47.840
This eye is the eye of a dead man.
Dead men can see through life

59:47.920 --> 59:51.640
like it was a curtain that billows
with the flicker of truth upon it.

59:51.720 --> 59:53.600
And I can see with this eye, Tommy,

59:53.680 --> 59:57.040
that your nephew is ascending
and he will be forgiven.

59:58.200 --> 59:59.360
Unlike you,

59:59.920 --> 01:00:01.960
who, on judgement day,

01:00:02.040 --> 01:00:05.280
is probably truly fucked
when the other shoe drops.

01:00:05.920 --> 01:00:06.760
[Alfie] Hmm?

01:00:10.920 --> 01:00:13.040
You all right, Tommy? How are you keeping?

01:00:15.200 --> 01:00:16.360
You know, Alfie,

01:00:17.760 --> 01:00:18.600
[clicks tongue]

01:00:18.680 --> 01:00:21.960
so many people, so many times,

01:00:22.880 --> 01:00:24.720
going to so much trouble to kill me.

01:00:25.880 --> 01:00:27.240
I'm fucking dying anyway.

01:00:27.720 --> 01:00:29.640
Well, we're all dying anyway.

01:00:29.720 --> 01:00:30.680
No.

01:00:31.800 --> 01:00:36.360
Not a bullet, not a bomb, not a knife.

01:00:37.000 --> 01:00:39.160
Is it clap? Is it clap?

01:00:39.240 --> 01:00:40.120
No.

01:00:40.800 --> 01:00:41.880
Not even that noble.

01:00:42.880 --> 01:00:45.440
[Alfie] What are you trying to say?
I'm about to sign over

01:00:45.520 --> 01:00:48.160
half of fucking Camden Town to you,
as part of the deal,

01:00:48.240 --> 01:00:49.880
and you're saying you're just gonna

01:00:49.960 --> 01:00:51.720
die in your bed?

01:00:52.600 --> 01:00:55.280
I'm not going to die in bed, Alfie.
Who fucking dies in bed?

01:00:55.360 --> 01:00:57.840
Good people die in their bed, Tommy.
Good people.

01:00:57.920 --> 01:00:59.480
-Good people, eh?
-Mmm.

01:01:00.960 --> 01:01:01.880
Good people.

01:01:02.680 --> 01:01:04.120
And yet here we are, Alfie.

01:01:05.760 --> 01:01:07.920
After all this time, just you and me.

01:01:10.840 --> 01:01:12.160
And I crossed the line.

01:01:16.120 --> 01:01:16.960
Michael…

01:01:19.760 --> 01:01:20.680
Polly…

01:01:23.280 --> 01:01:24.440
Ruby…

01:01:26.840 --> 01:01:32.680
Tommy, if you are about to
express profound emotion,

01:01:32.760 --> 01:01:37.040
you might be better served expressing it
to someone who gives a fuck.

01:01:37.800 --> 01:01:42.920
Or perhaps to somebody
who is being paid to pretend to have to.

01:01:43.000 --> 01:01:47.040
Like a fucking nurse or a priest. Someone.

01:01:49.600 --> 01:01:50.840
And, as for death,

01:01:51.880 --> 01:01:56.360
speaking as someone
who has been dead for a number of years,

01:01:56.440 --> 01:01:58.360
I can only heartily recommend it.

01:02:00.080 --> 01:02:01.120
Well, Alfie,

01:02:02.440 --> 01:02:04.280
your opera is complete.

01:02:07.680 --> 01:02:08.520
[sighs]

01:02:11.160 --> 01:02:14.400
Shall we go and witness the final act?

01:03:00.280 --> 01:03:01.720
Whenever you're ready, boys.

01:03:37.560 --> 01:03:38.760
[inaudible conversation]

01:03:44.920 --> 01:03:46.440
That's enough. [clears throat]

01:03:48.240 --> 01:03:49.680
Thank you all for coming.

01:03:51.520 --> 01:03:53.240
Well, at least I can say that, er,

01:03:54.960 --> 01:03:58.680
I am one of those rare politicians
who actually makes good on his promises.

01:04:00.720 --> 01:04:01.800
Country estate,

01:04:02.480 --> 01:04:06.040
requisitioned to make way
for houses for working people.

01:04:06.800 --> 01:04:09.880
I improved my own home
with good intentions

01:04:10.720 --> 01:04:12.480
and 1,500 pound of dynamite.

01:04:17.720 --> 01:04:19.120
Now I'm back where we began.

01:04:20.760 --> 01:04:22.280
With horses and caravans…

01:04:24.840 --> 01:04:25.960
vagabonds and thieves.

01:04:31.120 --> 01:04:32.480
Frances, sit down, please.

01:04:41.920 --> 01:04:43.240
I'd like to raise a toast.

01:04:45.040 --> 01:04:46.080
A simple toast.

01:04:49.840 --> 01:04:52.440
-To family.
-[man] To family.

01:04:53.000 --> 01:04:53.920
Sometimes,

01:04:55.560 --> 01:04:57.120
it is shelter from the storm.

01:04:59.000 --> 01:05:00.720
Sometimes, it is the storm itself.

01:05:11.920 --> 01:05:13.640
Planning on going away for a bit.

01:05:15.600 --> 01:05:16.600
After I'm gone…

01:05:20.840 --> 01:05:21.720
Ada,

01:05:23.160 --> 01:05:24.240
in this family,

01:05:25.640 --> 01:05:27.800
it was you who was
born to be a politician, not me.

01:05:29.960 --> 01:05:30.960
Remember that.

01:05:32.960 --> 01:05:37.320
And if ever a seat is to become available
in this ugly old city, you should run.

01:05:38.160 --> 01:05:39.120
[chuckles softly]

01:05:39.200 --> 01:05:40.360
[Tommy] Where's Arthur?

01:05:40.440 --> 01:05:42.560
[Linda] He went for a walk down the river.

01:05:43.240 --> 01:05:48.040
He said he's not good at farewells,
so he decided to go catch a trout instead.

01:05:51.560 --> 01:05:53.200
He told me to tell you that…

01:05:56.080 --> 01:05:58.480
"Where you're going, Tommy,
there will I be."

01:06:00.120 --> 01:06:01.120
"Very soon."

01:06:01.720 --> 01:06:02.720
"Love, Arthur."

01:06:09.760 --> 01:06:12.080
How does Arthur know
where you're going, Tommy?

01:06:14.520 --> 01:06:15.600
You watch him, Linda.

01:06:16.960 --> 01:06:17.960
You love him.

01:06:22.720 --> 01:06:23.680
Charles.

01:06:25.040 --> 01:06:26.760
I want you to look after your mum.

01:06:27.760 --> 01:06:29.600
You tell her I'm sorry, you hear me?

01:06:36.400 --> 01:06:37.600
I want you to be the…

01:06:42.600 --> 01:06:45.080
Exactly how long
are you going away for, Tommy?

01:06:56.680 --> 01:06:57.760
[Tommy] Thanks, Curly.

01:07:02.600 --> 01:07:03.800
[whispers inaudibly]

01:07:15.480 --> 01:07:16.760
[Curly] Tom, the horse…

01:07:17.360 --> 01:07:18.640
[Charlie] Shut up, Curly.

01:07:25.880 --> 01:07:27.440
[Tommy] Is she hitched, Johnny?

01:07:29.120 --> 01:07:31.640
Tommy, you tell me right now,
where are you going?

01:07:32.520 --> 01:07:35.280
You have to carry the bucket
on your own this time, Ada.

01:07:35.360 --> 01:07:37.920
Tommy, you come to me with everything.
You always come to me.

01:07:38.000 --> 01:07:40.640
Not this time. Not this one, sister.

01:07:40.720 --> 01:07:43.560
What the fuck does that mean?
Where are you going?

01:07:45.680 --> 01:07:46.680
Tommy!

01:07:50.040 --> 01:07:52.320
♪ My eyes are open wide ♪

01:07:54.440 --> 01:07:56.760
♪ And now I see you ♪

01:07:59.160 --> 01:08:01.640
♪ Without your robes on ♪

01:08:01.720 --> 01:08:02.760
[crow caws]

01:08:03.720 --> 01:08:06.040
♪ Without your crown ♪

01:08:16.080 --> 01:08:16.920
[caws]

01:08:18.440 --> 01:08:22.080
♪ I don't want to hate you ♪

01:08:22.160 --> 01:08:23.040
[exhales]

01:08:23.120 --> 01:08:26.080
♪ I don't want to bear ♪

01:08:27.840 --> 01:08:31.000
♪ The kind of fascination ♪

01:08:32.640 --> 01:08:35.600
♪ That gets in my way ♪

01:08:41.319 --> 01:08:43.800
♪ The door that opens wide ♪

01:08:46.080 --> 01:08:48.399
♪ My high up altar ♪

01:08:50.800 --> 01:08:53.240
♪ Oh heaven, help me ♪

01:08:54.760 --> 01:08:55.640
[grunts]

01:08:55.720 --> 01:08:57.840
♪ Is that the time? ♪

01:08:57.920 --> 01:08:58.920
[groans]

01:09:00.200 --> 01:09:02.439
♪ Beginning ♪

01:09:02.520 --> 01:09:04.240
♪ Without end ♪

01:09:04.840 --> 01:09:06.439
♪ Never lost ♪

01:09:07.160 --> 01:09:08.760
♪ Never die ♪

01:09:09.640 --> 01:09:11.200
♪ Unending ♪

01:09:11.279 --> 01:09:12.120
[horse snorts]

01:09:12.200 --> 01:09:13.080
♪ Beam of light ♪

01:09:14.319 --> 01:09:15.600
♪ A tunnel ♪

01:09:16.600 --> 01:09:19.279
♪ In my mind ♪

01:09:20.920 --> 01:09:23.600
♪ As it opens wide ♪

01:09:24.439 --> 01:09:27.399
♪ With a filter on the lens ♪

01:09:28.960 --> 01:09:31.960
♪ She sees everything I do ♪

01:09:33.760 --> 01:09:36.800
♪ She sees everything I do ♪

01:09:38.439 --> 01:09:41.479
♪ And without my shoes on ♪

01:09:43.080 --> 01:09:45.960
♪ Over broken glass ♪

01:09:47.720 --> 01:09:51.000
♪ I am dancing for pennies ♪

01:09:52.439 --> 01:09:56.640
♪ I am staring straight ahead ♪

01:10:01.120 --> 01:10:03.560
♪ A view that is so wide ♪

01:10:05.720 --> 01:10:07.680
♪ It's gonna break ♪

01:10:10.560 --> 01:10:16.320
♪ It's like it holds me in its gaze ♪

01:10:19.840 --> 01:10:21.160
♪ If I go ♪

01:10:22.200 --> 01:10:23.360
♪ It's because ♪

01:10:24.480 --> 01:10:28.200
♪ It's happened once before ♪

01:10:29.080 --> 01:10:34.960
♪ And now it's starting all again ♪

01:10:40.600 --> 01:10:43.080
♪ As it opens wide ♪

01:10:44.000 --> 01:10:46.800
♪ Forget everything you knew ♪

01:10:48.480 --> 01:10:51.440
♪ Forget everything you knew ♪

01:10:53.160 --> 01:11:00.040
♪ As it opens wide ♪

01:11:02.520 --> 01:11:05.760
♪ Like a newborn child ♪

01:11:07.200 --> 01:11:10.200
♪ Like a newborn child ♪

01:11:11.880 --> 01:11:14.680
♪ Like a newborn child ♪

01:11:16.680 --> 01:11:19.480
♪ A child ♪

01:11:21.240 --> 01:11:22.760
♪ A child ♪

01:11:24.520 --> 01:11:25.360
[gun clicks]

01:11:25.960 --> 01:11:28.680
♪ A child ♪

01:11:30.680 --> 01:11:33.240
♪ Like a child ♪

01:11:35.360 --> 01:11:37.560
♪ A child ♪

01:11:58.680 --> 01:12:02.120
[Tommy] In the bleak… midwinter.

01:12:06.240 --> 01:12:07.720
[Ruby] Dad, come outside!

01:12:09.240 --> 01:12:10.400
Dad, it's me.

01:12:25.240 --> 01:12:29.600
Did Polly send you? Did Polly send you?

01:12:31.080 --> 01:12:32.680
Or am I dead already?

01:12:32.760 --> 01:12:33.720
[Ruby] No.

01:12:35.880 --> 01:12:36.960
You're not dead.

01:12:38.320 --> 01:12:39.840
You're not even sick.

01:12:40.520 --> 01:12:42.000
But I am, my darling.

01:12:43.960 --> 01:12:44.960
I am sick.

01:12:46.520 --> 01:12:47.720
Sick like you was.

01:12:48.240 --> 01:12:49.640
No. Not true.

01:12:50.200 --> 01:12:52.640
I know it. You've got to live, Daddy.

01:12:55.880 --> 01:12:57.120
You let the fire go out.

01:13:00.400 --> 01:13:05.320
Light the fire again and get warm,
and you will see that you must live.

01:13:11.680 --> 01:13:12.800
[Tommy sighs]

01:13:22.320 --> 01:13:23.480
[sniffs]

01:13:29.920 --> 01:13:30.760
[twigs snapping]

01:14:08.240 --> 01:14:10.600
-[Ruby] You're not even sick, Daddy.
-[horse grunts]

01:14:25.000 --> 01:14:26.080
[toilet flushes]

01:14:32.680 --> 01:14:33.520
[magazine thuds]

01:14:47.480 --> 01:14:49.360
Fucking Gypsies.

01:14:57.760 --> 01:14:59.760
Have you thrown
the tinkers off the top field yet?

01:14:59.840 --> 01:15:02.760
No. I went to the caravan, sir,
but there was no one there.

01:15:02.840 --> 01:15:05.160
Go back up there
and set fire to the fucking thing.

01:15:05.240 --> 01:15:06.080
Yes, sir.

01:15:13.080 --> 01:15:14.880
Have you filled the car with petrol?

01:15:17.680 --> 01:15:18.640
[metallic clunking]

01:15:22.840 --> 01:15:25.920
I said, have you
filled the car with petrol?

01:15:26.000 --> 01:15:26.840
[grunting]

01:15:29.400 --> 01:15:30.920
How was the wedding in Berlin?

01:15:34.040 --> 01:15:36.800
I hear Chancellor Hitler himself
was the best man.

01:15:39.040 --> 01:15:42.160
You've been my doctor now for three years.

01:15:43.880 --> 01:15:45.880
I never knew you were so well connected.

01:15:46.560 --> 01:15:48.480
Oh, and the doctor at St Thomas',

01:15:49.480 --> 01:15:52.680
who you sent me to for the second opinion,
second set of X-rays.

01:15:53.560 --> 01:15:55.520
A maid of honour at the same wedding.

01:15:56.640 --> 01:15:58.760
Also very well-fucking-connected.

01:15:58.840 --> 01:16:00.600
[Holford breathes shakily]

01:16:01.080 --> 01:16:02.320
On your knees, Holford.

01:16:03.240 --> 01:16:04.120
[Holford exhales]

01:16:08.680 --> 01:16:10.960
I'm guessing you people all decided

01:16:11.040 --> 01:16:15.280
that the only person
who could ever kill Thomas Shelby

01:16:16.720 --> 01:16:18.240
is Thomas Shelby himself.

01:16:21.840 --> 01:16:24.080
You made me believe death was coming.

01:16:24.960 --> 01:16:26.760
Let my nature do the rest, eh?

01:16:31.960 --> 01:16:34.120
You may not have tuberculoma, Mr Shelby,

01:16:35.880 --> 01:16:37.080
but you are sick.

01:16:38.520 --> 01:16:39.520
I know you.

01:16:40.920 --> 01:16:42.160
You are sick with guilt.

01:16:44.960 --> 01:16:47.800
Sick of death at your own hand.

01:16:49.360 --> 01:16:50.720
Sick of who you were.

01:16:53.840 --> 01:16:57.920
You are no longer the kind of man
who would kill another man in cold blood.

01:17:03.960 --> 01:17:07.200
Tommy, you have been on a journey.

01:17:08.160 --> 01:17:11.000
From the back streets
to the corridors of power.

01:17:13.840 --> 01:17:15.280
You can't go back.

01:17:17.400 --> 01:17:18.680
You are a different man.

01:17:20.640 --> 01:17:22.640
The gun no longer belongs in your hand.

01:17:29.840 --> 01:17:31.120
Oh, but I am back.

01:17:34.160 --> 01:17:35.640
Back from under the ground.

01:17:38.320 --> 01:17:43.880
Close your eyes. Close your eyes.

01:17:47.720 --> 01:17:49.000
[bell tolls]

01:17:49.840 --> 01:17:51.240
[Holford whimpering]

01:18:08.040 --> 01:18:09.080
The eleventh hour.

01:18:11.360 --> 01:18:12.280
Armistice.

01:18:15.720 --> 01:18:21.600
Peace at last. Peace at last.

01:18:24.880 --> 01:18:26.520
-[gunshot rings]
-[Holford gasps]

01:18:33.680 --> 01:18:34.920
[Holford sighs]

